==============================================================================
THE CONTRAST (why the residual needs opus's structured lane, not measure)
==============================================================================
At band 2/25, seven combs have total danger measure 7*4/25 = 28/25 > 1:
with FREE phases the adversary CAN tile the circle (free fraction -> 0).
But the family's OWN phases (u_i t0 at a base-clear t0) avoid the tiling.
  7 consecutive [1..7]: total danger measure 1.120; ADVERSARIAL min free fraction = 0.1100 (cannot tile even adversarially)
  7 primes: total danger measure 1.120; ADVERSARIAL min free fraction = 0.2510 (cannot tile even adversarially)
  pole-7-cluster: total danger measure 1.120; ADVERSARIAL min free fraction = 0.2340 (cannot tile even adversarially)
  => the >=7 residual is NOT a free-measure statement; the specific
     phase orbit {u_i t0 : t0 in G_B} is the object, and opus-S97's
     transport shows the RAY orbit hits margin 2/13 (>2/25) -- the
     unbounded direction is CLOSED; the non-ray patterns are finite.
